# Agent rule files written by `next dev`
#
# next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js writes AGENTS.md (and a CLAUDE.md
# that just @-includes it) into each app the dev server is run in, and re-adds
# the block if you delete it. There are eight Next.js samples here, so without
# this rule the tree goes dirty for whichever ones somebody happened to run.
#
# They are ignored rather than committed because this repo is published as
# reference material for customers: the block is tooling for whoever is editing
# the sample, not part of the sample. If we ever do want agent rules in here,
# they should be added deliberately to all eight, not left to whoever ran the
# dev server last.
#
# Negated at the repo root so a deliberate, hand-written CLAUDE.md for THIS
# repo still works — the generator only ever writes them inside an app
# directory, so the root is unambiguous.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md

